# TOON token stats

```elixir
Mix.install([{:elixir_harness, path: "."}])
```

TOON wins on uniform rows, loses on deep nesting. The harness encodes
selectively: uniform tool defs and history as TOON, the rest as JSON.

```elixir
uniform = %{"tools" => for i <- 1..20, do: %{"name" => "tool#{i}", "description" => "does thing #{i}"}}
nested = %{"session" => %{"id" => "abc", "meta" => %{"deep" => %{"deeper" => [1, 2, %{"x" => 1}]}}}}
IO.inspect(ElixirHarness.Toon.stats(uniform), label: "uniform")
IO.inspect(ElixirHarness.Toon.stats(nested), label: "nested")
```

The `[N]{fields}` header doubles as a guardrail: truncated model output
fails strict decode and triggers a retry instead of executing garbage.
